{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And the idols.</b> יחלוף (it will pass away), יכרות (it will be cut down), and likewise all forms of חלף (Proverbs 31:5), upon which death applies, and close to it: חלף והלך לו (Song of Songs 2:11)." "<b>Kalil.</b> A word applicable to singular masculine and feminine and to plural, and the meaning is 'entire,' as in כליל תכלת (Exodus 28:31), כליל תהיה (Leviticus 6:16)." "And the yod of <b>יחלוף</b> returns to the revered Name."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The citations to Proverbs 31:5 and Song of Songs 2:11 follow the Hebrew text as given, though their exact relevance to the lexical argument is characteristically compressed.", 2 "The phrase 'returns to the Name' likely means the prefixed yod is to be read as a marker of the divine name, but the grammar is cryptic and translated literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:38.204704861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}